# Deny everything, then re-allow specific paths.
# A new file is invisible to git until it is listed below, so `git add -A`
# cannot sweep up a token or a key file that landed in the repo by accident.
*

!.gitignore
!README.md
!AGENTS.md

!macos/
!macos/**
!linux/
!linux/**

# Re-deny credential shapes even inside an allowed package. Later patterns win,
# so these override the allows above.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*_rsa
*_ed25519
*.kdbx
.env
.env.*
**/credentials
**/credentials.json
**/hosts.yml
**/.netrc
**/mcp.json
**/session.json
**/Preferences.xml
**/RustDesk.toml
**/RustDesk2.toml
**/password
**/.storage/
**/com.plexapp.plugins.library.db*
